<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms latest green rate devaluations.</title>
<headline>EU confirms latest green rate devaluations.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates of the Belgian franc, German mark, Dutch guilder and Austrian schilling will be devalued for the second time this week with effect from Thursday, the European Commission confirmed.</p>
<p>The Belgian franc green rate will devalue to 40.3103 per Ecu, from 40.2147, the mark rate to 1.95540, from 1.95076, the guilder to 2.19663, from 2.19067 and the schilling to 13.7562, from 13.7246.</p>
<p>The UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) earlier on Wednesday forecast the devaluations, which follow changes on Tuesday. They are a result of the relative strength of the Finnish mark.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
